kgs/atlas-search/\n├── atlas_search.py\n├── eval/\n│   ├── eval3.py\n│   ├── README.md\n│   └── fixtures/golden-311.json\n└── fixtures/\n    ├── gen_core_fixtures.py -> ../atlas_search.py\n    └── core-expectations.json (refreshed against the current reference)\n```\n\nThe fixture generator now loads the checked-in reference instead of the laptop home-directory copy. The eval docs retain source hashes and distinguish the corpus-specific runner from the generic Rust `atlas-eval` scorer.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- `~/atlas/v3-venv/bin/python -I pkgs/atlas-search/fixtures/gen_core_fixtures.py` — pass.\n- `python3 -I -m py_compile pkgs/atlas-search/atlas_search.py pkgs/atlas-search/eval/eval3.py pkgs/atlas-search/fixtures/gen_core_fixtures.py` — pass.\n- Source and repository `eval3.py` runs on the frozen corpus produced identical summary and all 311 rank records (corpus fingerprint verified; recall@10 142, MRR 0.2655).\n- `cargo test -p atlas-core` — pass: 42 unit, 5 parity, 11 shard, and 6 stage tests.\n- `cargo run -p atlas-core --bin atlas-eval -- fixtures/eval-smoke.json test` — pass. The smoke fixture is synthetic and is not evaluation evidence.\n\n## Merge Danger\n\n**Door:** Two-way\n\n**Blast Radius:** Atlas search reference/evaluation tooling only; no runtime service behavior changes.\n\n<!-- codesmith:footer -->\n---\n<a href=\"https://backend.blacksmith.sh/track/enable-autofix?expires=1796754476&installation_model_id=443529&pr_number=7775&ref=codesmith_pr_footer&repository=developing-today%2Fcode&return_to=https%3A%2F%2Fgithub.com%2Fdeveloping-today%2Fcode%2Fpull%2F7775&signature=bf6f407210bc468fa45bf929b198fe11b963e015fbda75fe5dd15f3e60643c2b\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark.svg\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-light.svg\"><img alt=\"Autofix with [code]smith\" src=\"https://pr-comments-assets.blacksmith.sh/codesmith/autofix-with-codesmith-dark-3x.png\" width=\"190\" height=\"28\"></picture></a>\n<sup><a href=\"https://app.blacksmith.sh/developing-today/codesmith/code/pr/7775?autoLogin=true&ref=codesmith_pr_footer\">Open in [code]smith</a> · Need help on this PR? Tag <code>@codesmith-bot</code> with what you need.</sup>\n\n<!-- codesmith:autofix:disabled -->\n<!-- /codesmith:footer -->\n\n<!-- This is an auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->\n\n<!-- coderabbit-ai-generated:v1 -->\n\n## Summary by CodeRabbit\n\n- **New Features**\n  - Added a command-line tool for hybrid full-text and vector search across Turso or local SQLite, with filters for content type, topic, project, client, date, and sensitivity.\n  - Search results can include grouped sessions, nearby chunks, parent messages, or readable text. A separate command retrieves chunk and session details.\n  - Added an evaluator for comparing full-text, vector, and hybrid search against a frozen query set.\n- **Documentation**\n  - Documented the evaluation datasets, reference tools, and how to run the baseline.\n\n<!-- end of auto-generated comment: release notes by coderabbit.ai -->","labels":[],"milestone":null,"active_lock_reason":null,"created_at":"2026-11-08T18:27:52Z","updated_at":"2026-11-11T16:37:30Z","closed_at":"2026-11-11T16:37:27Z","merged_at":"2026-11-11T16:37:27Z","merge_commit_sha":"27018e7f41e2e9446b87c028eaeeb09c9519ff60","assignee":null,"assignees":[],"requested_reviewers":[],"requested_teams":[{"id":7767549,"node_id":"T_kwDOAZNvF84AdoX9","url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549","members_url":"https://api.github.com/organizations/26439447/team/7767549/members{/member}","name":"codeowners","description":"Team Discussions: developing-today/code","permission":"pull","privacy":"closed","notification_setting":"notifications_enabled","html_url":"https://github.com/orgs/developing-today/teams/codeowners","re